One important observation about this implementation

Unlike many enterprise fraud systems, this implementation does not check whether the policyholder is already on the active watchlist before inserting a new record.

The flow is simply:

Fraud Confirmed
        │
        ▼
Read Claim
        │
        ▼
INSERT fraud_watchlist

There is no duplicate check such as:

SELECT *
FROM fraud_watchlist
WHERE entity_id = 'POL-987654'
AND status = 'Active';

This means that if update_watchlist_from_case() is triggered multiple times for the same confirmed fraud case, the system may create multiple active watchlist entries for the same policyholder unless the database enforces a uniqueness constraint. In a production-grade insurance platform, a common enhancement would be to perform this existence check first and only insert a new row if no active watchlist entry already exists.
